# Coupled Oscillators

> [!NOTE] Learning objective
> Connect the eigenvalues of the stiffness matrix to the normal-mode frequencies.

For equal masses $m$ and spring constant $k$,

$$
M\ddot{\mathbf{x}} + K\mathbf{x}=0, \qquad
K=k\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\ -1 & 2\end{bmatrix}.
$$

| Mode | Eigenvector | Frequency |
|---|---:|---:|
| In phase | $(1,1)$ | $\sqrt{k/m}$ |
| Out of phase | $(1,-1)$ | $\sqrt{3k/m}$ |

## Explore

```smd-chart
{
  "title": "Two normal modes",
  "x": { "min": 0, "max": 12.56, "label": "time" },
  "series": [
    { "name": "mass 1", "expression": "Math.cos(x) + r*Math.cos(Math.sqrt(3)*x)", "color": "#6750a4" },
    { "name": "mass 2", "expression": "Math.cos(x) - r*Math.cos(Math.sqrt(3)*x)", "color": "#006a6a" }
  ],
  "sliders": [
    { "name": "r", "label": "Out-of-phase mixture", "min": 0, "max": 2, "step": 0.05, "value": 0.5 }
  ]
}
```

## Verify numerically

```python
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

t = np.linspace(0, 4*np.pi, 500)
plt.plot(t, np.cos(t) + .5*np.cos(np.sqrt(3)*t), label="mass 1")
plt.plot(t, np.cos(t) - .5*np.cos(np.sqrt(3)*t), label="mass 2")
plt.xlabel("time")
plt.legend()
plt.grid(alpha=.2)
```
